From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:59:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Verify signed block preview aborts and preserves Stage proof
 gates

Add a pure preview suite using an authenticated synthetic parent and actual BIP340 CHECKSIG spend, plus an ordered transaction spending the signed parent output. Compare exact framing, roots, monetary state and charges with lower-level calculations and the separately sealed complete Stage boundary. Every preview Ready/failure must abort exactly once; all failure output fields and external parent coins remain unchanged.

Exercise invalid signatures and truthful absent inputs, coinbase and witness-variant duplicate-ID grammar, provider read/write/root failures and throws after mutation, host/configuration Inconclusive outcomes, count/byte/time/history/work/root caps, required ASERT drift and reversed dependencies. Prove Ready cannot bypass Stage PoW, and preserve deterministic-invalid versus operational failure-proof classifications. No invented unsupported opcode, accepted preview status or proof output.

Standalone CMake borrows the independently owned evaluator without copying or committing dependencies, and builds unchanged complete-block/CHECKSIG tests with the new preview suite. Frozen core 7c8ced2fc: Debug 3/3 pass in 0.41s and ASan+UBSan 3/3 pass in 1.20s. Only three new owned test/documentation files; no old golden, implementation or shared build edits, network adoption or node claim.
